### Create employee
# @name CreateEmployee
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
## TEST-HAS-BODY
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "jan.novak@example.com"
}

### Create second employee
# @name CreateSecondEmployee
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Mgr.",
    "name": "Eva",
    "surname": "Kovacova",
    "phone": "0900 333 444",
    "email": "eva.kovacova@example.com"
}

### Read the created employee back
# @name GetEmployee
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET http://localhost:5080/api/employees/{{CreateEmployee.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### List employees
# @name ListEmployees
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Accept: application/json
